VACA_Vision 0.2.0 - independent local variant

Based on View Assist Companion App (VACA), created by MSP1974 (Mark Parker),
and View Assist (VA), created by Dinki, with their respective contributors.
Their work is the foundation of this variant. They are not responsible for
Vision-specific changes and no endorsement is implied.

VACA: https://github.com/msp1974/ViewAssistCompanionApp
VACA integration: https://github.com/msp1974/ViewAssist_Companion_App
View Assist: https://github.com/dinki/View-Assist

Derived from the supplied V13Overlay, V13OverlayIntegration and Android 7.1.2
ES8 sources. Vision adds separate application/integration identities, a shared
display protocol, role-aware entities, voice integration, revised BLE setup,
and a matching picker companion. Original native VACA audio is excluded.

Retain all upstream LICENSE and NOTICE files. See standard/LICENSE,
overlay/LICENSE in the app source bundle;
the integration's Apache-2.0 license is retained in LICENSE.

The Display and Dot role interoperates with unmodified echo-dot-assist by
Julian Imhof (Gamer92000), https://github.com/Gamer92000/echo-dot-assist, MIT.
It retains upstream firmware ownership; Vision handles output routing and ducking.
The shared Sendspin output derives from the supplied V13Overlay renderer and
Sendspin protocol SDK; its license is retained at shared-output/sendspin-protocol/LICENSE
in the app source. AndroidX Media3 is Apache-2.0 licensed.
